# CI ↔ pre-commit parity

This repo currently has **no** `.github/workflows/` CI job and **no**
`.pre-commit-config.yaml`. Local quality is `make lint` / `make test` (and Cursor
stop hooks).

If you add CI or pre-commit later:

1. Mirror substantive `make` checks in both places.
2. Document new targets in `make/help.mk` (`.cursor/rules/makefile-help-sync.mdc`).
3. Prefer the same commands locally and in CI — do not invent a second parallel list.
